Subject: =?UTF-8?q?=E2=86=95=EF=B8=8F=20Reorder=20pinned=20threads=20in=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?the=20grouped=20sidebar=20by=20dragging?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- In the grouped sidebar (Group threads by project, the boringSidebarEnabled client setting) a pinned card above the folders can be dragged to another position among the pinned cards, the way a folder card moves within its folder. Before, pinned cards there only dragged out as composer context.
- The list item's projectFolder becomes dragGroup, "rows that reorder only among themselves": folder cards keep their project key, and grouped-mode pinned rows get SIDEBAR_PINNED_DRAG_GROUP, a key built from the sidebar marker prefix so it can never equal a project key. The ungrouped list sets no dragGroup, so its items, drop targets, collision ranking and projection are unchanged.
- resolveSidebarFolderDropTarget is renamed resolveSidebarGroupedDropTarget. For the pinned group it returns the pinned section with the pinned keys reordered by moving the dragged card to the target card's index (the same order the ungrouped list's resolveSidebarDropTarget gives for that drop) and the active order untouched; folder groups keep the existing mapping onto the whole active order.
- The drop goes through the unchanged planSidebarThreadDrop "reorder-pinned" plan, the reorderPinnedThread writes, the optimistic drop and the "Failed to reorder pinned threads" toast an ungrouped pinned reorder uses, so the order persists, syncs to other devices and shows the same in the ungrouped list.
- While a pinned card is dragged only the pinned cards slide aside; a drop target exists only while the pointer is between the top of the first pinned card and the bottom of the last one; the collision ranking considers only pinned cards. The sorting strategy and collision detection treat the pinned group exactly like a folder group.
- In grouped mode the drag limit at the top of the list no longer reserves room for the Pinned boundary label, which grouped drags never show, so the first pinned card can be dragged back to the top. The ungrouped limit is unchanged.
- Grouped mode still has no pin or unpin by drag: a pinned card cannot drop into a folder and a folder card cannot drop among the pinned cards. Snoozed, settled and working rows stay context-drag-only, the Pinned and Active boundary labels and section hints stay hidden, and dragging a card onto the composer still mentions it.
- The user guide's Group threads by project section says pinned threads can be dragged to reorder among themselves, but not into a folder.
- Extends ↕️ Reorder threads inside project groups by dragging; squashed into it at the next carry.

