Tests:
- apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.logic.test.ts: the grouped dragging case now also has three grouped pinned cards; dragging p3 onto p1, p1 onto p2 and p1 onto p3 plans "reorder-pinned" with exactly the plan the equivalent ungrouped pinned drop gets (p3 onto p1 stores [p3, p1, p2]), a drop on the card's own place plans nothing, and a pinned card over a folder card, a settled row or the pinned divider, and a folder card over a pinned card, resolve no target.
- apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.drag.test.ts: the projection case shows that dragging a pinned card shifts only the pinned cards by the card height plus gap (up and down) and that hovering a folder card, a settled row or the divider moves nothing. The collision case selects a pinned card with the pointer inside the pinned extent, keeps the dragged card when grabbed near its bottom edge, and selects nothing just below the last pinned card or over a folder card.
- The new assertions fail on 81028ee903 (old Sidebar.logic.ts and Sidebar.drag.ts with only the names mapped): all three extended cases fail at the pinned assertions.
- vp test run Sidebar.logic.test.ts Sidebar.drag.test.ts: 182 passed. Sidebar.browser.test.tsx and SidebarThreadRow.browser.test.tsx: 13 passed.
- vp run check:changed HEAD (6 files): format, lint, knip 1/2 and 2/2, typecheck of 2 packages, tests (8 files, 212 passed plus the cross-file run) and the React compiler check passed.
- No browser-level drag test (no existing harness drives sidebar drags) and no run in a real client.

